---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How SidJam Studio handles information on this website and in our in-house tools.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <span class="kicker">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: November 22, 2026</p>
  </section>

  <div class="about prose">
    <p>
      SidJam Studio is a small independent studio based in the Bay Area. We keep privacy simple:
      we collect as little as possible, and we never sell or share personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't use analytics, advertising trackers or cookies, and the site has no accounts or sign-up forms.</li>
      <li>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages and loads fonts from Google Fonts. Like any web host,
        those services may log basic technical details such as your IP address and browser type,
        under their own privacy policies.
      </li>
      <li>
        The basket on our Designs page is saved only in your own browser (local storage) so it
        survives a page reload. It isn't sent to us until you choose to send your order by WhatsApp or email.
      </li>
      <li>
        Card payments are handled by Stripe on Stripe's own checkout page. We never see or store your
        card number; Stripe shares the payment amount, your order code and contact details with us so we
        can match your payment to your order.
      </li>
      <li>If you email or WhatsApp us, we use your message and contact details only to handle your order and reply to you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>SidJam Studio Trends (our internal tool)</h2>
    <p>
      We run a private, in-house research tool that helps us decide what designs to make for our
      t-shirt shop. It is used only by our studio and is not offered to anyone else.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>What it accesses:</strong> with our own Pinterest business account, it reads
        Pinterest Trends keyword data (for example, which search terms are growing in the US),
        plus basic details of our own account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What it doesn't do:</strong> it doesn't post, pin or change anything on Pinterest. It
        doesn't access other people's accounts, boards, Pins or personal information.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Storage:</strong> trend keywords and their growth numbers are stored on our own
        computer for design research. Access tokens are kept privately on that computer and never
        shared.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sharing:</strong> we don't sell, rent or share this data with anyone, and we don't
        use it for advertising.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deletion:</strong> we can disconnect the tool and delete stored data at any time.
        You can also revoke app access in your Pinterest settings.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Our stories are written for young readers, but this site doesn't knowingly collect any
      personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, we'll update this page and its date. For any privacy question, write
      to <a href="mailto:hello@sidjamstudio.com">hello@sidjamstudio.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
